    "text color" : "[0.0]",
    "content" : "(4) We can assume a ≠ 0 and a ≠ 1, because otherwise b = 1 or b = 0 respectively, and the thesis holds. We can also assume that c  ⩽ b, because otherwise b∨c = b↝µb↑. Let x1 > b and x2 > b such that (x1∧x2) > b and ((b∨c)∧xk) > b, for each k. The latter condition is equivalent to b∨(c∧xk)> b, which is equivalent to c∧xk ⩽  b. We need to show that"
  }, {
    "type" : "paragraph",
    "pdfua_tag" : "P",
    "id" : 31,
    "page number" : 1,
    "bounding box" : [ 251.519, 316.706, 343.751, 347.18 ],
    "font" : "MnSymbol12",
    "font size" : 11.955,
    "text color" : "[0.0]",
    "content" : "(b∨c)∧x1 ∧x2 > b,"
  }, {
    "type" : "paragraph",
    "pdfua_tag" : "P",
    "id" : 32,
    "page number" : 1,
    "bounding box" : [ 54.599, 288.614, 540.621, 324.14 ],
    "font" : "TeXGyreTermesX-Regular",
    "font size" : 11.955,
    "text color" : "[0.0]",
    "content" : "which is equivalent to c∧x1 ∧x2  ⩽ b. Since b is a pseudo-complement of a in L, c∧x1 ∧x2  ⩽ b holds if and only if"
  }, {
    "type" : "paragraph",
    "pdfua_tag" : "P",
    "id" : 33,
    "page number" : 1,
    "bounding box" : [ 256.68, 261.146, 338.591, 291.62 ],
    "font" : "MnSymbol12",
    "font size" : 11.955,
    "text color" : "[0.0]",
    "content" : "a∧c∧x1 ∧x2 ≠ 0."
  }, {
    "type" : "paragraph",
    "pdfua_tag" : "P",
    "id" : 34,
    "page number" : 1,
    "bounding box" : [ 54.6, 196.705, 540.748, 271.1 ],
    "font" : "TeXGyreTermesX-Regular",
    "font size" : 11.955,
    "text color" : "[0.0]",
    "content" : "Now, consider the elements a,x1,x2 ∈ L. a∧x1 ∧x2 ≠ 0 because otherwise we would have x1 ∧x2 ⩽ b, as b is a pseudo-complement of a. Moreover c∧xk ≠ 0 for each k, because otherwise we would have c∧xk ⩽ b. Finally c∧a ≠ 0, because otherwise c ⩽ b, contradicting our assumption. As c is a µ-element in L, we conclude that c∧a∧x1 ∧x2 ≠ 0, which proves the claim."
  }, {
