    "font size" : 11.955,
    "text color" : "[0.0]",
    "content" : "Remark 3.16. — An analogue of part (2) of Proposition 3.15 does not hold for upsets. Consider the frame of power set P(X) of the set X = {1,2,3,4,5}. We have {1,2}↝µ{1}↑ and {3,4}↝µ{3}↑, by Remark 3.12. However, it is easy to see that {1,2}∨{3,4} = {1,2,3,4} is not a µ-element in {1,3}↑ = {1}∨{3}↑. Moreover, it is also not a µ-element in P(X)."
  }, {
    "type" : "paragraph",
    "pdfua_tag" : "P",
    "id" : 40,
    "page number" : 1,
    "bounding box" : [ 54.6, 84.746, 540.685, 129.859 ],
    "font" : "TeXGyreTermesX-Italic",
    "font size" : 11.955,
    "text color" : "[0.0]",
    "content" : "Proposition 3.17. — Let L be a frame, a ∈ L, and b a pseudo-complement of a in L. If c ∈ L is maximal relative to the properties a ⩽ c and b∧c = 0, then a↝µc↓."
  } ]
